This reproduced incorrect ordering for both different labels and identical labels
in the two configs; it was not merely a unit test of numeric ordering fields.
The final fixtures exercise the actual scan and production comparator, including:
- Absent, unknown, explicit later-position, and excluded defaults.
- Conflicting label names and repeated label names across configs.
- Non-default source/declaration order after defaults, including filtered labels.
- The secondary config when the primary is absent, empty, or has no usable entry.
- A surviving secondary default ahead of non-preferred primary survivors.
The new multi-source fixture reverses scan output before sorting so insertion-order
stability cannot make the test pass accidentally.

